<article class="env-lemma" id="0G60">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G60">Lemma <span data-tag="0G60">92.10.3</span>.</a> Let $p$ be a prime number. Let $A \to B$ be a ring homomorphism and assume that $p = 0$ in $A$. If $A$ and $B$ are perfect, then $L_{B/A}$ is zero in $D(B)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map $(F_ A, F_ B) : (A \to B) \to (A \to B)$ is an isomorphism hence induces an isomorphism on $L_{B/A}$ and on the other hand induces zero on $L_{B/A}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0G5Z" data-tag="0G5Z">92.10.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>